          {"id":"e4e75adb","elType":"widget","widgetType":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p><strong>Bilona</strong> is a 3,000-year-old Vedic process that requires no machinery and no shortcuts.</p><p>Here is how every jar of Burans Valley A2 Bilona Ghee is made:</p><ol style=\"line-height:2;padding-left:20px;\"><li>A2 milk is collected from our desi cows in Uttarakhand.</li><li>The milk is gently cultured overnight to make curd.</li><li>The curd is hand-churned with a wooden <em>mathani</em> using a hemp rope — no electricity, no motors.</li><li>The <em>makkhan</em> (white butter) that rises is separated.</li><li>The makkhan is slow-cooked over a wood fire until pure golden ghee forms.</li></ol><p>[ADD: founder note or sourcing detail about your specific farm / Uttarakhand location.]</p>"}}
        ]},
